#!/bin/sh
# ssh to host y: every call is recorded in $HOME/.calls; y's engine API answers each
# call from answers/ssh/api-y/<call>.json, its Hello naming those calls: its create
# makes the VM linux-1, which its fleet answer holds.
answers="${0%/*}/../answers/ssh"
printf 'ssh %s\n' "$*" >> "$HOME/.calls"
case "$*" in
    *" station engine attach")
        terminated=''
        while [ $# -gt 0 ]; do
            case $1 in
                --) shift; terminated=1; break ;;
                -[BbcDEeFIiJLlmOoPpQRSWw]) shift 2 ;;
                -*) shift ;;
                *) break ;;
            esac
        done
        target=$1
        shift
        while [ -z "$terminated" ] && [ $# -gt 0 ]; do
            case $1 in
                --) shift; break ;;
                -[BbcDEeFIiJLlmOoPpQRSWw]) shift 2 ;;
                -*) shift ;;
                *) break ;;
            esac
        done
        if [ "$1" != sh ]; then
            echo "stub ssh: the far shell was given: $*" >&2
            exit 97
        fi
        far="$answers/api-$target"
        [ -d "$far" ] || exit 255
        version=$(/bin/cat "$far/version" 2>/dev/null)
        calls=$(cd "$far" && for f in *.json; do printf '"%s",' "${f%.json}"; done)
        while IFS= read -r line; do
            id=$(printf '%s' "$line" | /usr/bin/jq -r .id)
            call=$(printf '%s' "$line" | /usr/bin/jq -r '.call // empty')
            if [ -z "$call" ]; then
                printf '{"v":2,"id":"%s","hello":{"version":"%s","calls":[%s]}}\n' "$id" "$version" "${calls%,}"
            else
                printf '{"v":2,"id":"%s","out":%s}\n' "$id" "$(/bin/cat "$far/$call.json")"
            fi
        done
        ;;
    *)
        echo "stub ssh: unexpected invocation: $*" >&2
        exit 97
        ;;
esac
